    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** leading the charge, boasting an elite 75.13 score against Pfaadt. He serves as our strongest play, buoyed by a favorable matchup and a solid park factor. Joining him at the top of the board is **Jacob Wilson** (72.17) and **Andy Pages** (72.12). **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from wind blowing out and a favorable SP xERA of 4.13, while **Andy Pages** finds himself in an advantageous spot against Pfaadt, where his aggressive approach and favorable batting order position maximize his expected production. **Jackson Merrill** (65.93) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.46) also remain locked in as strong starts, though **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** requires close monitoring due to a 30% rain risk at his venue.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was separating **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** from our lower-tier starters. **Sam Antonacci** (43.60) was the primary candidate for promotion, but he ultimately fell short due to the sheer dominance of Williams on the mound, which suppressed his overall ceiling compared to the primary lineup. We also continue to track **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to navigate the middle infield with depth options like **Nasim Nunez** (48.97). While **Nasim Nunez** provides a boost in SB potential\u2014a core pillar of our strategy\u2014his production is capped by a difficult matchup against Burns.\n\nManagers should remain alert regarding the **Liam Hicks** slot; his 47.11 score assumes a #4 spot in the order, and any deviation from that projection could force a re-evaluation of his utility. Conversely, we are avoiding the temptation to play **Heliot Ramos** (47.64) against the elite arm of Sale. Despite Sale's reputation, **Heliot Ramos** maintains a marginal grade, but we are prioritizing the higher efficiency of our other outfielders today. We remain confident that the combination of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and the rest of our core provides the necessary balance of power and speed to maintain our standing in the Roto standings.",
